{{!< default}}
{{!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     custom-signin.hbs — ported from NSDS templates/signin-form.html.
     ------------------------------------------------------------------------
     A Ghost CUSTOM TEMPLATE: create a page in Ghost Admin and pick "Signin"
     in the editor's template dropdown. The file name after `custom-` is what
     the dropdown shows, which is the whole of the wiring.

     ── WHY THIS EXISTS WHEN PORTAL ALREADY DOES IT ─────────────────────────
     Ghost's Portal is an overlay: it opens over whatever page you were on
     and has no URL of its own worth linking. That is right for "sign in
     while reading" and wrong for everywhere sign-in is the DESTINATION — an
     emailed link, a bookmark, a nav item, a 403 bounce. Those need a page.

     The navbar keeps using Portal (partials/navbar/auth.hbs, data-portal),
     because there the reader is mid-task and should not lose their place.
     Two doors to the same room, and neither is a reimplementation: both
     hand off to Ghost Members.

     ── data-members-* IS GHOST'S OWN CONTRACT, NOT A STYLE HOOK ────────────
     Ghost's members bundle binds [data-members-form] on every page and does
     the whole exchange: POST to /members/api/send-magic-link/, then toggling
     [data-members-success] / [data-members-error]. NSDS's archetype already
     carries those attributes — its comment says so — so the port is markup
     only. There is NO JavaScript in this theme for it, and there must not
     be: a second implementation of an auth flow is how you get an auth flow
     that works in one of two places.

     ⚠ Both state blocks ship `hidden`. Ghost unhides the right one. Remove
     the attribute and every visitor is told to check an inbox nothing was
     sent to.
     ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ --}}
<div class="ns-auth">
    <div class="ns-auth__card">
        <p class="ns-auth__kicker">{{t "sign in"}}</p>
        <h1 class="ns-auth__title">{{#if title}}{{title}}{{else}}{{t "Sign in"}}{{/if}}</h1>
        <p class="ns-auth__sub">{{t "Enter your email and we will send you a sign-in link. No password needed."}}</p>

        <form class="ns-auth__form" data-members-form="signin">
            <div class="ns-field">
                <label class="ns-field__label" for="ns-signin-email">{{t "Email address"}}</label>
                <input id="ns-signin-email" class="ns-input" type="email" name="email"
                       autocomplete="email" required data-members-email>
            </div>
            <button class="ns-btn ns-btn--primary ns-btn--block" type="submit">{{t "Send sign-in link"}}</button>

            <div class="ns-auth__sent" data-members-success role="status" hidden>
                <p class="ns-auth__sent-title">{{> "icons/check-circle"}} {{t "Check your inbox"}}</p>
                <p>{{t "Open the link we sent to finish signing in."}}</p>
            </div>
            <p class="ns-field__error" data-members-error role="alert" hidden>
                {{t "We could not find an account for that address."}}
                <a href="{{@site.url}}/signup/">{{t "Create one instead"}}</a>.
            </p>
        </form>

        <p class="ns-auth__alt">{{t "New here?"}} <a href="{{@site.url}}/signup/">{{t "Create an account"}}</a></p>
    </div>
</div>
